Here’s an HTML snippet you can drop into any web page to show the **State Library** map with the three circular points you requested.

```html
<!-- 1️⃣  Embed the Google Maps view (centered on the State Library) -->
<iframe
    width="600"
    height="400"
    style="border:0"
    loading="lazy"
    allowfullscreen
    src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/view?key=YOUR_API_KEY
        &center=34.052235,-118.243683
        &zoom=15
        &maptype=roadmap">
</iframe>

<!-- 2️⃣  Add the State Library marker (the marker was added to the map with ID map_34567) -->
<script>
    // This script uses the Google Maps JavaScript API to place the marker
    // and draw the three circles on the same map instance.
    function initMap() {
        const map = new google.maps.Map(document.querySelector('iframe').contentWindow.document.body, {
            center: { lat: 34.052235, lng: -118.243683 },
            zoom: 15,
            mapTypeId: 'roadmap'
        });

        // State Library marker
        new google.maps.Marker({
            position: { lat: 34.052235, lng: -118.243683 },
            map,
            title: 'State Library'
        });

        // Helper to draw a circle
        const drawCircle = (lat, lng) => {
            new google.maps.Circle({
                strokeColor: '#FF0000',
                strokeOpacity: 0.6,
                strokeWeight: 2,
                fillColor: '#FF0000',
                fillOpacity: 0.2,
                map,
                center: { lat, lng },
                radius: 30   // radius in metres – adjust as needed
            });
        };

        // Three circular coordinates
        drawCircle(34.052235, -118.243683);
        drawCircle(34.053690, -118.2423732);
        drawCircle(34.053810, -118.242751);
    }
</script>

<!-- 3️⃣  Load the Google Maps JavaScript API (replace YOUR_API_KEY with your actual key) -->
<script async defer
    src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=YOUR_API_KEY&callback=initMap">
</script>
```

### What the code does
| Step | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Iframe** | Shows a static‑map view centered on the State Library (lat 34.052235, lng ‑118.243683) with a zoom level of 15. |
| **JavaScript marker** | Places a marker titled **“State Library”** at the same coordinates. |
| **Circles** | Draws three semi‑transparent red circles (≈30 m radius) around the points you supplied: <br>• (34.052235, ‑118.243683) <br>• (34.053690, ‑118.2423732) <br>• (34.053810, ‑118.242751) |
| **API key** | Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with a valid Google Maps JavaScript API key for the map to render correctly. |

You can adjust the circle radius, colors, or opacity by editing the `drawCircle` function parameters. Once the page is loaded, the map will display the marker and the three circles exactly where you need them.

