Below is the **exact snippet you need** to make every typing‑animation run at **300 words‑per‑minute** while keeping the default *1 second* start‑delay.

```html
<script type="module">
  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  // 1️⃣  Set the global typing‑animation defaults
  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  //  • delayBeforeStart is omitted → the library will use its default (1000 ms)
  //  • typingSpeed is set to 300 wpm as you requested
  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  await functions.setTypingAnimation({
    typingSpeed: 300          // 300 words per minute
    // delayBeforeStart: 1000 // ← not needed – defaults to 1000 ms
  });

  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  // 2️⃣  Now initialise the SVG for each input you want to animate
  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  async function attachTypingAnimation(inputSelector, opts = {}) {
    const input = document.querySelector(inputSelector);
    if (!input) throw new Error(`No element matches ${inputSelector}`);

    // Merge the global speed (300 wpm) with any field‑specific options
    const api = await initTypingForInput(input, {
      typingSpeed: 300,          // enforce 300 wpm for this field as well
      ...opts
    });

    // …rest of the wiring (same as the full example in the previous answer)…
    // (listen to input, blur/focus, etc.)
    return api;
  }

  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  // 3️⃣  Initialise on page load (example for a field with id="name")
  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    attachTypingAnimation('#name', {
      fontColor: '#333',
      fontSize: 16,
      deletionSpeed: 250,          // optional – keep your preferred delete speed
      pauseBeforeRetyping: 200
    });
  });
</script>
```

### What this does

| Action | Effect |
|--------|--------|
| `functions.setTypingAnimation({ typingSpeed: 300 })` | Sets the **global typing speed** to **300 wpm**. Because we didn’t pass `delayBeforeStart`, the library keeps its built‑in default of **1000 ms** before the first character appears. |
| `initTypingForInput(..., { typingSpeed: 300 })` | Guarantees that any field‑specific SVG you create also inherits the 300 wpm speed (some libraries let you override per‑SVG). |
| The rest of the code (event listeners, pause/resume, deletion animation) works exactly as described in the previous answer. |

You can now drop this script into any page that already includes the `functions` namespace, and every form‑field typing animation will start after the default 1‑second pause and type at **300 words per minute**. 🎉

